BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.08 0.18 0.38 rg 56.00 258.39 Td (Q8. Explain the exact mathematical formula used to calculate the Risk Score.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.20 0.25 rg 50.00 231.39 Td (The Risk Score is a transparent heuristic ranging from 0 to 100 points, calculated as:) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.20 0.25 rg 56.00 213.89 Td (1. Speeding Points \(max 45\): speeding_ratio * 45.0) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.20 0.25 rg 56.00 202.39 Td (2. Harsh Braking Points \(max 20\): min\(harsh_braking_count / max\(distance_km / 10, 1\), 1.0\) *) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.20 0.25 rg 50.00 190.89 Td (20.0) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.20 0.25 rg 56.00 179.39 Td (3. Harsh Acceleration Points \(max 20\): min\(harsh_acceleration_count / max\(distance_km / 10,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.20 0.25 rg 50.00 167.89 Td (1\), 1.0\) * 20.0) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.20 0.25 rg 56.00 156.39 Td (4. Night Driving Points \(max 15\): night_driving_ratio * 15.0) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.20 0.25 rg 50.00 138.89 Td (Total Points = clip\(Speeding + Braking + Acceleration + Night, 0, 100\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.20 0.25 rg 50.00 127.39 Td (Final Score = floor\(Total Points + 0.5\) to produce an integer score.) Tj ET
